From 2526e754e162e6708046a3e4c8403f13898f042c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omesh <roland@nordhain.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 09:25:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] grpc-stream: opt-in cmake infrastructure + skeleton
 client (no logic yet)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 1c step 1 — adds the build wiring for the cuprate gRPC streaming sync
client. Skeleton implementation only; methods return false / no-op so the
target compiles cleanly and we get a sanity check on the build setup before
the real client lands in step 2.

Build is opt-in via -DMONERO_ENABLE_GRPC_STREAM=ON. Default OFF — existing
build setups are completely unaffected.

Build deps when enabled:
  macOS: brew install grpc cmake
  Linux: apt install libgrpc++-dev libprotobuf-dev protobuf-compiler-grpc

CMake design notes:
- New static library cuprate_grpc_stream lives under src/wallet/grpc_stream/.
  Wallet links it conditionally (target_link_libraries(wallet PRIVATE
  cuprate_grpc_stream) in CMake; #if MONERO_GRPC_STREAM in source).
- Pimpl-wrapped client (grpc_block_stream_client.h) keeps grpc++ headers OUT
  of wallet2's translation unit. Wallet2 only sees a bare header that uses
  std types, so the existing Boost-Asio + epee build stays clean of
  abseil/grpc ABI.
- Uses pkg-config (grpc++, grpc, protobuf) instead of find_package(gRPC
  CONFIG): the CMake-config path imports a modern protobuf::libupb target
  set that conflicts with the vintage protobuf Monero pulls in via Trezor
  device support. pkg-config sidesteps the imported-target machinery and
  just hands us include paths + library names — no double-import error.
- Bumps CXX_STANDARD to 17 just for the cuprate_grpc_stream target — modern
  abseil headers (which grpc++ depends on) use std::is_same_v et al.
  Monero's default of C++14 stays intact for everything else.

Verified locally on macOS 26 (AppleClang 17, gRPC 1.80, protobuf 34.1):
configure clean, `make cuprate_grpc_stream` builds the library cleanly
(only deprecation warnings out of upstream grpc++ headers). Default-OFF
build path (no flag) untouched.

Real client implementation (channel + recv thread + bounded queue +
extensive PERF logging) lands in the next commit.
